{"version":1,"key":"card:651","content":{"id":651,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"791f097d-a9f0-401c-bb29-82b7e8a94859","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"破窗效应是犯罪心理学上一个著名的理论：如果对环境中的一个小问题不及时修复，这个小问题就会暗示此处环境没人管，从而造成更大的混乱。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"ff2d8363-b14d-47ad-aba7-e9d9e40a1a1f","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"在 1982 年三月的《大西洋周刊》上，犯罪心理学家詹姆斯·Q·威尔逊及乔治·凯林发表了一片《Broken Window》的文章，两位作者为了阐述无序的环境会导致犯罪，举了一个例子："}]},{"type":"blockquote","tauContract":"751ccba427a94db9cea481a017ab0a4e94033bd3aa16d3496b70412fe6baf04b","collabId":"3284075d-736f-4b44-ac14-c03880dd52e4","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"31576989-071e-444c-9acb-fe8a58536091","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"试想一幢建筑，如果有一扇窗户破了（Broken Window），且迟迟没有人去修补。路人看到后就会觉得：这里没人管，没人负责。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"dff0d987-6ecb-412f-970f-1bca6e6f358b","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"很快，其他的窗户也会被打破。既然没人管，那么哪怕是打破更多的窗户、甚至闯入建筑内搞破坏，也不会受惩罚。这扇没人修的「破窗」，就是混乱的开始。"}]}]},{"type":"image","url":"http://blog-hostimaging.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/image_e7b46637-7046-4820-b447-b6f2cd0dc1f6.webp","uuid":"a0d4cd5a-19b9-43b6-aaee-9de6ca5da98b","pasteUploading":false,"previewUrl":"http://blog-hostimaging.oss-cn-beijing.aliyuncs.com/image_e7b46637-7046-4820-b447-b6f2cd0dc1f6.webp","width":701.0848473108825,"tauContract":"9d766f08643a09b151c9500b642decb7d9f8625878621cbd90af820668058ac0","collabId":"b34a3ee4-7cbe-4d0f-8320-fd0225b5eab5","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":""}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"a29982b5-ef8a-4ef4-b011-11a8b503430c","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"由于这个比喻深入人心，因此大家就用破窗效应（Broken Window Theory）来指代这一套理论。"}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"e393227c-e969-4df9-9a78-85e82363da15","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"在我们的生活中也经常会看到一些破窗效应："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","tauContract":"b74d37e5bfbf2503c151b31f93763a8fb42e80426564246cbb0af72201a60e8c","collabId":"12c54219-cbcf-4e30-83b9-a9ac167f901f","children":[{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"a2764868-1e97-403c-a385-08efa416fdfa","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"e0dacc5b-59bf-4ec1-9f5c-a907b4c1a283","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"为了减肥你每天都进行运动，突然有一天下雨，你中断了（破窗），第二天没有及时补上，你心理就会想，反正都中断了，不如歇一天吧，最终会导致彻底放弃"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"76faca24-e13e-40e9-8d46-9c185d8117af","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"b709fb1a-4d2c-4f13-ad5c-1d9687502a7a","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"家里卫生本来很干净，只有偷懒一次，桌子上的易拉罐、卫生纸没有及时清理（破窗），那么就会暗示你可以不整理卫生，导致垃圾越堆越多，成为垃圾堆"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"a41cc009-3279-43c7-8a98-a8ae6847a104","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"破窗效应给我们带来的启示就是"},{"type":"formatted","bold":true,"text":"防微杜渐"},{"type":"formatted","text":"："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","tauContract":"b74d37e5bfbf2503c151b31f93763a8fb42e80426564246cbb0af72201a60e8c","collabId":"0b976897-ed46-4f7b-b5a0-c8f0176e6413","children":[{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"2df692f6-7411-45a9-9c3e-0b8d7f8969ba","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"ee4d658f-7882-43ad-96f9-8b9481885dde","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"对于管理者/家长：当看到第一扇窗被打破时（员工迟到、孩子撒谎），要及时进行修补，表明态度"}]}]},{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"19fee757-7f5b-4072-a393-4ef18804f0c3","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"361a3433-8492-406c-a36a-6bde5000e091","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"对于个人：不要轻易打破第一扇窗，不要想着「仅此一次，下不为例」，这一次往往就是溃败的开始，"},{"type":"content-link","contentId":4900,"contentType":"card","contentTitle":"","refId":649,"tauContract":"720a42c66441f65bfc897253311b73deb687a68a60da46dffe8c7b8537a65760","collabId":"054867cd-1b1a-49ff-a1c9-599a38fedda9","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"就像是在滑梯顶端迈出的一步"}]},{"type":"formatted","text":"，一旦迈出，就会随着重力沿着滑梯不断下降，直至走向彻底的混乱"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"fb5cc31e-2f97-454a-af03-b3bf31090ace","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"参考："}]},{"type":"bulleted-list","tauContract":"b74d37e5bfbf2503c151b31f93763a8fb42e80426564246cbb0af72201a60e8c","collabId":"6b3f5bba-587f-4e59-a8d2-952719106cdb","children":[{"type":"list-item","tauContract":"fe3a1fc1f6dcf1c1c317754db368a19bd85cab343431da98cae17d783eaa1c02","collabId":"1d59a66a-09c4-4f21-99f7-797bdaf651e4","children":[{"type":"paragraph","disableDrag":false,"tauContract":"f4b9b0426991dbd09af21b77c91da8b4112b2e3901b6af87feb71cb3b7772fb1","collabId":"f3afecb0-f6e2-43d0-91a7-a168648fabc8","children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%A0%B4%E7%AA%97%E6%95%88%E5%BA%94","openEdit":false,"tauContract":"ebf1d56e356279ad64279a16e90d9b28280f70eac20d5071950fc0c4b5c364a6","collabId":"7933ef70-47ae-45ab-ac70-69e6110f46ba","children":[{"type":"formatted","text":"破窗效应"}]}]}]}]}],"tags":["心理学/破窗效应"],"createTime":1767143210066,"updateTime":1777355948261,"linkedCards":[]},"meta":{"type":"card","publishTime":1777355948261},"links":{"card:649":{"key":"card:649","type":"card","id":649}}}